index 20a87b4..875379d 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -6,6 +6,12 @@ Small command-line tool the ops team uses to summarise event logs exported from
 
 prints one line per service and level with the number of events, then a total.
 
+To look at recent events only, pass `--since` with a date or ISO 8601 datetime:
+
+    python -m evlog report events.jsonl --since 2024-03-10
+
+This counts events at or after that time. A bare date means midnight UTC. A value with an offset (for example `2024-03-10T09:00:00+09:00`) is converted to UTC. A value without an offset is UTC. An invalid `--since` value is reported as a usage error (exit code 2). A missing or unreadable events file exits with code 1.
+
 Each line of an events file is a JSON object:
 
     {"ts": "2024-03-09T23:30:00-05:00", "service": "api", "level": "error", "msg": "upstream timeout"}
